From c8c0bbd263b7031b3f966433583c931f1fd5108a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: eatradish <sakiiily@aosc.io>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 18:31:45 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/8] BACKPORT: FROMLIST: feat(oma): make D-Bus optional and
 split AOSC profiles

Add a `dbus` feature that pulls in zbus and all D-Bus integration.
Without it, oma and oma-pm compile no zbus code: battery/wake-lock
checks, logind detection, instance lookup, and amo status reporting are
removed instead of being skipped at runtime.

Move the shared AOSC integration into `aosc-common`, then define two
parallel profiles: `aosc` (common + D-Bus) and `afterglow` (common
only). Enabling `afterglow` with `aosc`/`dbus` is a compile error, so
Afterglow builds use `--no-default-features --features
"openssl-setup afterglow"`.

Co-authored-by: DeepSeek <noreply@deepseek.com>

[ Mingcong Bai: Resolved minor merge conflicts in ...
    oma-pm/Cargo.toml
    src/config.rs ]

Link: https://github.com/AOSC-Dev/oma/pull/880
Signed-off-by: Mingcong Bai <jeffbai@aosc.io>
---
